References: 
https://patents.justia.com/patent/8102393
https://patents.justia.com/patent/6476807

Qualcomm style POS in 2 passes to generate a visibility stream but this uses different hardware, iGPU for Culling and dGPU for Replay
https://patents.justia.com/patent/8102393

It is also "RunAhead" not all in one like Qcomm. Essentially its a culling mechanism, not a Tiled Rendering mechanism

It appears to be outputing the visibility stream from the Pixel shader (Render Target)

You could technically do this purely in SW too, like your depthPrePass. Just have the fragment shader output a bitstream and use that to predicate draw call indices. Is there such a thing possible?


https://patents.justia.com/patent/8102393
Background section provides a good description on why Occlusion Queries (stalling and predicated(conditional rendering) ones are not so great)


Occlusion Queries can be useful for a very Coarse Grained approach


https://patents.justia.com/patent/8564616
Adds shader based frustum culling and clip plane tests along with Position fetch (and optionally, attributes required to do the test, fetch)

If the first pass is not trivially rejected for a batch of 32 indices, then it proceeds with the second phase (fetch all attributes and do the vertex shading)

I don't know if they do backface culling. Also does not have a provision for a Coarse Grained Rasterization, pre-HiZ etc...
